Practitioners of Occultism look to Eanna, the noble daughter of the governor of Delphinad and a kind-hearted, selfless soul. A symbol of mercy and power, she would later become the goddess Nui.

'''Occultism''' is a magic damage and crowd control [[Skill Trees|skill tree]] that wears enemies down over time. It turns mana into damage, drains life from its targets and pins them down with impales, silences and suspensions. It is usually paired with trees that add burst damage, healing, utility and more crowd control.

== Skills ==
=== Combat skills ===
{{TreeSkills|Occultism|combat}}

=== Passive skills ===
Passives cost 1 skill point each and unlock after you have spent the listed number of points in Occultism.
{{TreeSkills|Occultism|passives}}

=== Abyssal skills ===
The [[Abyssal Skills]] have to be unlocked through a questline and don't require skill points to be used.
{{TreeSkills|Occultism|abyssal}}

